        <OtherAbstract Type="PIP" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>Of a group of 93 cases of extrauterine pregnancy, 10 women, aged 20-40, had IUDs at the point of conception. None of these patients had had an ectopic pregnancy before. 6 of the women had copper IUDs. Although none of the patients had had IUD related symptoms before, the pain and bleeding which occurred were diagnosed in most cases as IUD side effects. All patients eventually underwent unilateral salpingectomy. As side effects of IUD use can also be symptoms of ectopic pregnancy, care must be taken in diagnosis.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
